  description: Terbium is a chemical element with symbol Tb and atomic number 65.
    It is a silvery-white rare earth metal that is malleable, ductile and soft enough
    to be cut with a knife. Terbium is never found in nature as a free element, but
    it is contained in many minerals, including cerite, gadolinite, monazite, xenotime
    and euxenite.
